# Aito predictive database connection
# Get your credentials at https://aito.ai
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Single-tenant — one Aito DB serves the whole demo (PetNord).
# Multi-tenant routing was deliberately dropped vs. aito-erp-demo;
# this demo is one persona, one DB, one set of fixtures. See
# docs/adr/0001-scaffold-and-stack.md.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
AITO_API_URL=https://shared.aito.ai/db/aito-ecommerce-demo
AITO_API_KEY=your-api-key-here

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# R&D environment — keep experiments off the shared/prod instance
#
# The instance above is SHARED: the deployed demo (ecommerce.aito.ai)
# and anyone running locally point at the same DB. Critically, the
# Layer-2 prediction cache is a table ON that instance, so running
# experimental code against it (re-pointed queries, new tables) writes
# cache rows the deployed app then serves — cross-contaminating prod.
#
# For R&D, create your own Aito instance and override the connection in
# `.env.local` (gitignored; sourced after .env by `./do`, so it wins):
#
#   # .env.local
#   AITO_API_URL=https://shared.aito.ai/db/aito-ecommerce-dev
#   AITO_API_KEY=your-dev-instance-key
#
# Then `./do reset-data` rebuilds your dev instance from the
# deterministic fixtures (seed=42) — an exact copy of prod to mutate
# freely. The cache lives on the dev instance, so prod is never touched.
# `./do load-data|reset-data|clear-cache|warm-cache` print the target
# instance (and flag the shared one) so you always know which you hit.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Public-demo lockdown (set when deploying to ecommerce.aito.ai)
#
# PUBLIC_DEMO=1 enables:
#   - CORS lockdown to the origins listed in CORS_ORIGINS
#   - /api/schema returns 404 (don't leak the table layout)
#   - Two-tier rate limiting (per-IP + global)
#   - Memory-only cache (works with a read-only Aito API key)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
PUBLIC_DEMO=
CORS_ORIGINS=https://ecommerce.aito.ai
RATE_LIMIT_PER_IP=60
RATE_LIMIT_GLOBAL=1500
